  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e0e83d5f270870d48ac3fc737eb0c586, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tireur
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryTitle: Tireur
  listOfTextEntry:
  - As a general rule, these demons show a remarkable ability to adapt to the mechanical
    elements of their environment. However, even with this aptitude, it seems that
    the "shooters" remain at the bottom of the demonic hierarchy.
  - Possessing excellent vision, they seem to watch their surroundings attentively,
    letting no prey escape...
  - Metallic legs, prosthetics resembling human limbs
  - Emaciated physique
  - Human-sized
  - In combat, they seek distance by all means
  - Their movements are stiff and unbalanced, likely due to their prosthetics...
  - You can find torn-off arms similar to theirs not far from mechanical equipment.
    It seems they deliberately mutilate themselves to "enhance" themselves.
  - The weight difference of the cannon has a significant impact on the shooter's
    balance, especially when firing. They receive an excessive recoil that prevents
    them from having a higher rate of fire.
  - It seems that the cannon replacing one of their limbs is the result of an assembly
    of different human mechanisms, but its logic remains beyond my understanding
    despite my studies.
